                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.aop/1048516535"} Euclid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Kapranov"}> Mikhail Kapranov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Noncommutative geometry and path integrals
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebra, Arithmetic and Geometry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0612411"} arXiv:math/0612411
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+B%C3%A4r"}> Christian Bär
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Pf%C3%A4ffle"} Frank Pfäffle
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Path integrals on manifolds by finite dimensional approximation
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AP/0703272"} arXiv:math.AP/0703272
            %li
              %p
                Dana Fine,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+F.+Sawin"} Stephen F. Sawin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Rigorous Path Integral for Supersymmetric Quantum Mechanics and the Heat Kernel
                %strong 284
                (2008) 79–91 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0705.0638"}> arXiv:0705.0638
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-008-0606-2"} doi:10.1007/s00220-008-0606-2
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (for
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetric+quantum+mechanics"} supersymmetric quantum mechanics
            %li
              %p
                Florian Hanisch,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthias+Ludewig"} Matthias Ludewig
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Rigorous Construction of the Supersymmetric Path Integral Associated to a Compact Spin Manifold
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.10027"} arXiv:1709.10027
          %p
            A discussion for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+spaces"} phase spaces
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+polarization"} Kähler polarization
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Charles99
              Laurent Charles,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Feynman path integral and Toeplitz Quantization
              %strong 72
              (1999) 341., (
              %a{:href => "http://ipht.cea.fr/DocsphtV2/articles/t98/093/public/publi.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            following
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Norris92"} Norris 92, theorem (34)
          %h3#more More
          %p Other references on mathematical aspects of path integrals include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Cartier"}> Pierre Cartier
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%C3%A9cile+DeWitt-Morette"} Cécile DeWitt-Morette
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Functional integration: action and symmetries
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511535062"} doi
            %li#HenneauxTeitelboim
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Henneaux"}> Marc Henneaux
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Teitelboim"} Claudio Teitelboim
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantization+of+Gauge+Systems"} Quantization of Gauge Systems
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nikolai+Reshetikhin"}> Nikolai Reshetikhin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on quantization of gauge systems
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1008.1411"} arxiv/1008.1411
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A new look at the path integral of quantum mechanics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1009.6032"} arxiv/1009.6032
          %p
            Detailed rigorous discussion for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+Hamiltonians"} quadratic Hamiltonians
            and for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            paths in in
          %ul
            %li#RobbinSalamon93
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joel+Robbin"}> Joel Robbin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dietmar+Salamon"} Dietmar Salamon
              %em Feynman path integrals on phase space and the metaplectic representation
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dietmar+Salamon"} Dietmar Salamon
              (ed.),
              = succeed "," do
                %em Symplectic Geometry
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/RobbinSalamonMetaplectic.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of quantization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            via a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wiener+measure"} Wiener measure
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Adrian P. C. Lim.
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  Chern-Simons Path Integral on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
                  Using Abstract Wiener Measure
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-analysis/volume-11/issue-2/Chern-Simons-Path-Integral-on-R3-Using-Abstract-Wiener-Measure/cma/1298669952.full"} Euclid
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=MR2780879"} MR2780879
          %p
            Lecture notes on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AJ+Tolland"}> AJ Tolland
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.sunysb.edu/~ajt/Teaching/560spring2011/"} Wilsonian QFT for Mathematicians
          %p
